The container looks like a paper bowl or plate about 15–16 cm across at the rim. The almonds fill most of the inner area, roughly 11–12 cm across, and are piled about 2–3 cm deep.

An almond is about 1.2 g, and the pile looks like roughly 70–80 almonds. That gives about 85–95 g. A loose pile of almonds has a bulk density of about 0.6 g/cm³. The volume is roughly a spherical cap with a 12 cm diameter and 3 cm height, about 170 cm³, which comes to about 100 g. I'll use 90 g.

